WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.560
The project is called Cities and Human

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.560
Society in the 21st Century,

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.530
and the logic is pretty simple.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.740
About 800 million people

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.620
will be added in
cities all over the world

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.840
in the next 2 decades

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.720
or so and within 20, 25 years

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.640
we'll have 60
cities over

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.970
10 million inhabitants.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:28.130
Cities are the leaders of our globalizing
world and they are the Avant garde of all

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.130
this transformation.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:34.210
So we need to really take care of them and
to understand how to deal with that.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:35.860
These are places where you have an

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.000
immense concentration of

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.900
power, wealth, talent, cultural movement,

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.540
innovation going on.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:49.780
And then the thing about these 4 areas that
makes sense for us, cyber change and the post-carbon

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.120
city, Big Data, and all the new data and knowledge
that we can produce.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:01:01.440
The social division inclusion of cities, and
the infrastructure and housing.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.100
Bringing people together from different urban
experiences and getting them to talk to one

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:11.639
another, and getting them to think about how
the evidence that I know from one setting

00:01:11.639 --> 00:01:16.310
might be similar to, but also might be different
from the evidence that comes from another

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:23.920
setting is potentially a way also of thinking
outside the box and changing what the box is.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.869
So to do that you need something like CIFAR
which is unique in its capacity to provide

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:33.619
a framework where you bring those people from
different background together to think about

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.060
knowledge that might be transformative.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:43.220
And as a result the impact will hopefully
be that each of the disciplines will become

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:47.980
more powerful by interacting with the other
disciplines.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:54.980
Successful cities will make for a successful
21st Century human society as a whole and

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:00.500
that's really our goal and our deep commitment,
and to do it at a planetary or global scale.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:08.420
[Music]

